title: Config options
section: Reference
desc: Every option of bddr.config.ts with its type, default and a link to where it is explained.
lede: All options go at the top level of defineConfig, and every one except profiles can be changed for one run with --set.
---
<h2>Specs and steps</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>features</code></td><td>string or string[]</td><td><code>features/**/*.feature</code>, <code>features/**/*.feature.md</code></td><td>Spec globs, relative to the config file.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>steps</code></td><td>string or string[]</td><td><code>steps/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}</code>, <code>features/**/*.steps.{ts,js,mjs}</code></td><td>Support code: steps, hooks, fixtures, parameter types.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>dataDir</code></td><td>string</td><td>the config folder</td><td>Folder for <code>@data:</code> files. With a profile, <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/&lt;profile&gt;/file</code> is tried first.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>language</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>'en'</code></td><td>Default Gherkin language.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>plugins</code></td><td>array</td><td></td><td>Package names, file paths, <code>[name, options]</code> pairs or plugin objects. See <a href="plugins.html">How plugins work</a>.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>Selection and values</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>tags</code></td><td>string</td><td></td><td>Tag expression applied to every run. Combined with <code>-t</code> using and.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>string</td><td></td><td>Regular expression on the scenario name.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>params</code></td><td>Record&lt;string, string&gt;</td><td></td><td>Values for <code>ctx.params</code>. <code>-D</code> overrides.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>Execution</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>workers</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Scenarios running at once.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>pool</code></td><td><code>'inline'</code> or <code>'process'</code></td><td><code>'inline'</code></td><td>See <a href="process-pool.html">Worker processes</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>groups</code></td><td>Record&lt;string, GroupConfig&gt;</td><td></td><td>See below and <a href="groups.html">Groups</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>defaultMode</code></td><td><code>'parallel'</code>, <code>'serial'</code>, <code>'exclusive'</code></td><td></td><td>How ungrouped scenarios run.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>featureMode</code></td><td><code>'parallel'</code> or <code>'serial'</code></td><td></td><td><code>'serial'</code> runs the scenarios of every feature in file order. <code>@parallel</code> opts a feature out.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>failFast</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Stop after the first failed scenario.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>strict</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Pending, undefined and ambiguous steps fail the run.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>Time and retries</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>stepTimeoutMs</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>30000</code></td><td>Default step and hook timeout. <code>0</code> turns it off.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>scenarioTimeout</code></td><td>duration</td><td></td><td>Time budget per scenario attempt, such as <code>'2m'</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>runTimeout</code></td><td>duration</td><td></td><td>Time budget for the whole run, such as <code>'30m'</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>retry</code></td><td>object</td><td></td><td><code>{ scenario, delay, backoff, workerCrash, on, failOnFlaky }</code>. See below.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>A duration is a number of milliseconds or a string such as <code>'500ms'</code>, <code>'2s'</code>, <code>'1m'</code>.</p>

<h3>retry</h3>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>scenario</code></td><td>Extra attempts for a failed scenario.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>delay</code>, <code>backoff</code></td><td>Wait between attempts, and the factor it grows by.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>workerCrash</code></td><td>Retries on a fresh process after a worker crash.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>on</code></td><td>Only retry errors that match. An entry matches the error name exactly, the message as a substring, or a regular expression written as <code>'/text/'</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>failOnFlaky</code></td><td>Fail the run when a scenario passed only after a retry.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h3>groups.&lt;name&gt;</h3>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>'parallel'</code> (default), <code>'serial'</code> or <code>'exclusive'</code> (alone in the run).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>workers</code></td><td>The most members running at once.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>dependsOn</code></td><td>Groups that must finish first.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>onDependencyFailure</code></td><td><code>'skip'</code> (default) or <code>'run'</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>priority</code></td><td>Lower starts first.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>locks</code></td><td>Locks every member holds.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>match</code></td><td>A tag expression that adds scenarios to the group.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>retry</code>, <code>retryMembers</code></td><td>Re-run the whole group up to n times. <code>'all'</code> (default) or <code>'failed'</code> members.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>scenarioRetry</code></td><td>Default scenario retry for members.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>timeout</code></td><td>Time budget for one attempt of the group.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>Output</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>reporters</code></td><td>array</td><td></td><td>See <a href="reporters.html">Reporters</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>logLevel</code></td><td><code>'debug'</code>, <code>'info'</code>, <code>'warn'</code>, <code>'error'</code>, <code>'silent'</code></td><td><code>'info'</code></td><td>Console log level. Events always contain every log.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>history</code></td><td>boolean or <code>{ dir, keep }</code></td><td></td><td><code>true</code> keeps the last 50 runs in <code>.bddr/history</code>. Dry runs are never recorded.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>validation</code></td><td>object</td><td></td><td><code>{ allowedTagKeys: string[] }</code> for tag checks in <code>bddr validate</code>.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>profiles</h2>
<p><code>profiles</code> maps a name to a partial set of the options above. It cannot be changed with <code>--set</code>. See <a href="profiles.html">Profiles and --set</a> for how profiles merge.</p>
